A||||7||Pyric||My Exhaust has dimples!||||1||
Z||000000||Pyric||11-26-2001||05:28 PM||||Okay, here is the deal.  My exhaust has been glowing pretty bright and I think I've pinpointed the problem and have ordered the parts for it.  However...<P>I have stock Manifolds on it and I've noticed that there is a slight indentation above each T in the manifold where the valves blow the exhaust into the pipe.  Is this normal?  <P>I honestly never paid enough attention to it before it started glowing, so I don't remember what it used to look like.<P>Anyone know?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mickey_Moose||11-26-2001||05:55 PM||||those 'indents' are normal...they usually like to crack near the welds in those locations however  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pyric||11-26-2001||06:18 PM||||That's a relief.  I was worried that they were getting hot enough to start melting.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Loki||11-26-2001||07:35 PM||||If they were getting THAT hot you have WAY more problems and more than likely not a car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/lokisig1%20copy.jpg">  <BR>"All Fieros broke right now" :(||||reg||1
Z||000004||hugh||11-26-2001||08:49 PM||||It sounds like your timing is retarded.||||reg||7
Z||000005||Pyric||11-26-2001||11:16 PM||||Yeah, maybe... but I just had the timing done.  I ordered some steel vacuum lines and I'm going to check the EGR tube when I have the intake off.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I got the car with a brand new engine in it, the last owner just could not get it to run without problems.  <P>He said the exhaust got so hot it melted the wire to the fuel pump in two before he dropped the new engine in.  It had gotten so hot it had blown oil through the head gasket. I helped him tear it out, and there were lumps of charcoal (formerly oil) everywhere.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>It idled very rough when I got it, and now that I fixed that problem the exhaust is glowing again.  <P>I want to make sure it's running right before I take it for a drive.  I don't need any more coal in my engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||tesmith66||11-27-2001||12:40 PM||||You have a cracked EGR tube and possibly cracked vacuum lines. I have seen the glowing manifolds on my car and the EGR tube fixed it. Get one from a 2.8 liter firebird at a junkyard. Mine was only a buck and all I had to do was elongate the mounting holes on one end with a Dremel tool.<P>Keep an eye on those exhaust manifolds. They WILL crack at the flange and they WILL leak. Take them off, have each flange welded completely around the outside of the tube, grind all of the obstructions away from the inside of the tubes, replace ALL of the studs and bolts, and you will never have to worry about them again. You will also pick up a few (5-7) horsepower from the increased flow.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good luck, and welcome to the V6 Fiero experience.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe<p>[This message has been edited by tesmith66 (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000007||Pyric||11-27-2001||01:36 PM||||Thanks,  Hopefully this will fix it.  I've been chasing this problem for a while and keep getting distracted by other problems it causes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
